# Rianell security & privacy

## Never commit these files

- `security/.env` or root `.env` — Supabase credentials
- `security/.encryption_key` — encryption key material
- `supabase-config.js` — contains API keys
- `apps/pwa-webapp/models/**/onnx*` — ONNX weights are gitignored; weights live in Supabase Storage only

## API key rules

- Frontend code always uses the **publishable / anon key** (`SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`)
- **Never** use the `service_role` key in client-side code
- Pool insight RPCs must have `REVOKE EXECUTE ON FUNCTION … FROM anon`; `GRANT EXECUTE` to `authenticated` only

## Health data (GDPR Art. 9)

- Health data requires explicit user consent before processing or upload
- Screening responses (PHQ-9/GAD-7) must **never** be written to logs, IndexedDB, AsyncStorage, or Supabase
- Anonymised data sharing is opt-in only (`dataSharing` preference)
- Smartlook session recording is off by default; SDK must not load until user opts in

## E2E encryption

- Exports use PBKDF2 + AES-GCM (`P4` feature)
- Passphrase-derived DEK wrapping via `keyManagement.mjs`
- AsyncStorage is encrypted via `secureStorage.mjs` (Plan 21)

## CI supply-chain

- Run `npm audit` and `pip-audit` before deploy
- `scripts/verify/verify-csp-connect-src.mjs` must pass before any CSP change ships
- Gitleaks runs on every CI push; new secrets in `i18n-packs/` or `tier-a-exact-overrides.mjs` must be added to `.gitleaks.toml` allowlist
